From b82e570a43a0de4a74ad1701d9c4984c253587f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your Name <you@example.com>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 08:07:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add Ollama LLM classification for They Live slogans

Instead of picking a random phrase, the content script now extracts
ad context (text, img alts, aria-label, link URLs) and sends a batched
request to the background service worker.  The service worker calls the
Ollama /api/chat endpoint with a categorisation prompt and returns the
best-fit phrase; elements are updated from their random placeholder the
moment the LLM responds (~250 ms batch window).

New message handlers in background.js:
- theyLiveClassify: calls Ollama, returns phrase per ad context
- getTheyLiveSettings / setTheyLiveSettings: read/write storage keys
  theyLive.ollamaEnabled, .ollamaUrl, .ollamaModel, .ollamaApiKey

Dashboard settings panel lets the user enable Ollama, set the URL
(default http://localhost:11434), model (default llama3.2) and an
optional Bearer API key.  The fields are hidden while the toggle is off.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
