From 892b7c5760d3868825fc5f54bd096ac05b92cfab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your Name <you@example.com>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 08:25:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Add deep thinking toggle for Ollama classification
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a 'Deep thinking' checkbox in the They Live AI settings panel.
When enabled, the Ollama API request includes `think: true`, activating
chain-of-thought reasoning on models that support it (e.g. qwq,
deepseek-r1). For models that don't support the flag it is silently
ignored.

Disabled by default — thinking adds latency without benefit for simple
phrase classification. Users can opt in for models where it matters.

Changes:
- dashboard.html: add #theyLiveThinking checkbox in #theyLiveOllamaFields
- background.js: read theyLive.ollamaThinking, spread think:true when set;
  include ollamaThinking in get/setTheyLiveSettings handlers
- settings.js: wire thinkingEl to load/save logic

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
